  "verbalization": "Genistein is implicated in targeting multiple entities, including 30S ribosomal protein S4 and Shiga-like toxin 1 subunit B, which in turn target Replicase polyprotein 1ab. This suggests that genistein may exert its effects through diverse molecular pathways, potentially influencing viral replication processes. The evidence points to a possible role of genistein in modulating viral replication by targeting components of the ribosome or other cellular machinery involved in viral protein synthesis. The integration of these pathways highlights the potential for genistein to interact with viral components, possibly through indirect mechanisms that involve cellular targets. While the exact mechanism remains unclear, the observed relationships suggest that genistein may act as a modulator of viral replication, though further investigation is needed to elucidate the precise molecular interactions.",
